module engine where

-- derive-traversable — the generic, schema-directed `traverse` (the Traversable
-- half of the FP-derivation arc, unified-static-analysis Phase 6d).
--
-- Any `* -> *` type WITHOUT an authored `Traversable` instance gets `traverse`
-- (and `sequenceA` over it) for FREE: a single always-on structural `Traversable`
-- instance keyed by `{$pattern:"engine:isUnaryConstructor"}` resolves through the
-- SHIPPED `matchStructural` substrate, and its `traverse` is `engine:deriveTraverse`
-- — a thin category-B reflection+marshal bridge (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts) that
-- (a) resolves the dispatched value's owning type + marshals its schema across the
-- `$`-key barrier via `marshalTraversalType`, and (b) RESOLVES THE APPLICATIVE `g`
-- (D-6d-2 — see below) and threads `g`'s `pure`/`ap` handles into THIS body. The
-- authored `Maybe`/`List`/`Result` instances keep nominal precedence
-- (`resolveStructural` is the last fall-through).
--
-- traverse : (a -> g b) -> f a -> g (f b). Walk the structure `f a`, apply the
-- effectful `f`-arg to each element (an `a`, producing a `g b`), SEQUENCE the
-- effects with the applicative `g`, and rebuild the structure inside `g`.
--
-- THE EMPTY-APPLICATIVE / RETURN-POSITION `pure` PROBLEM (D-6d-2). In the
-- empty/leaf case, `traverse` must return `pure (empty structure)` in `g`. But
-- `g` is determined by the RETURN type of the effectful function `a -> g b`, NOT
-- by any runtime value (Fenel dispatches on values; Haskell resolves this by
-- TYPES). The resolution: the bridge resolves `g`'s `pure`/`ap` (from the
-- function's declared return type — the SOUND path that also covers the empty
-- case — with a non-empty first-element reflection fallback) and threads them in
-- as `pureFn`/`apFn`. So THIS body never guesses `g`: the empty case is just
-- `pureFn $ value`, and a field is sequenced with `apFn`. An unresolvable
-- all-empty-over-an-opaque-closure case is the bridge's documented fence, never a
-- silently-wrong applicative.
--
-- THE REBUILD (the generic, sound accumulator). `acc` starts as `pureFn $ value`
-- (the ORIGINAL value, in `g`) — so `$tag` + every NON-traversed field survive
-- automatically. For each field that DOES traverse (element / self-recursive /
-- nested functor), produce its `g`-wrapped new value `gNew` and combine:
--   acc' = ap (fmap (\v nv -> assocRecord v fldName nv) acc) gNew
-- i.e. lift a one-field SETTER over the accumulator (`g (nv -> value)`), then
-- `ap` it against `gNew` (`g nv`) ⇒ `g value'`. This handles ANY arity / shape,
-- and the empty/no-traversable-field case is exactly `acc = pureFn $ value`.
-- `fmap` resolves `g`'s own Functor by dispatch (nominal for `Maybe`/`List`/
-- `Result`, derived for a user functor); `pureFn`/`apFn` are the threaded handles.
--
-- TOTALITY (D-6d-5): descend ONLY into strictly-smaller self-recursive sub-values;
-- an unknown tag / non-record value / unrecognised field-type ⇒ `pureFn $ value`
-- (never crash). FENCE (D-6d-4): one-level nested foreign functor (`Wrap (List a)`
-- ⇒ a `TtApp` arg carrying the param) re-dispatches `Traversable.traverse`;
-- COMPOUND nesting (`List (Box a)`) is LEFT (treated as a non-traversed field),
-- documented, never silently mis-handled.
--
-- `$map`-FIELD DESCENT (D-6c-3 CLOSED, array-substrate Phase 1a). A `TtMap` field
-- whose VALUES carry the functor param (`Map String a`) is TRAVERSED by
-- `mapTraverse f` over the field value — the `Traversable (Map k)` operation
-- (`g (Map k b)`), combined onto the accumulator via the same `deriveTraverseAp`
-- as the nested-functor arm. A direct call, NOT a `Traversable.traverse`
-- re-dispatch (a bare map field has no `$tag` to dispatch on — the Phase-1a
-- Step-0 fact). COMPOUND map values (`Map String (Box a)`) stay LEFT (D-6d-4).
--
-- Closure-apply uses `$` (`($) f x = f x`): the binop/handles are closure- or
-- fnId-valued, applied via `$` (`(apFn $ setterG) $ gNew`) — the algebra-methods
-- convention. std fns (`mapGet`/`assocRecord`/`eq`/`head`/`tail`/`concat`/`map`)
-- are called by bare codeName (the engine-body idiom). All helpers are prefixed
-- `deriveTraverse…` to avoid registry collisions with the deriveFmap…/deriveFoldr…
-- families.

-- deriveTraverse — the bridge's declaration, so the nominal Traversable
-- instances (std/algebra-instances.fenel) can hold it as the reference
-- `engine.deriveTraverse`. Its native is a context native of the
-- `derive-functor` container (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts `deriveFunctorModule`),
-- so it runs only in a registry that carries that container (the engine
-- harness, the derive-* tests). Two parameters, `traverse`'s arity. The return
-- is `Any`, not a type variable: the native returns either the traversed value
-- inside the applicative or, when it cannot resolve the applicative, its input
-- unchanged, and a free result variable would let a caller pick any type for
-- that (`consumeString (deriveTraverse f 7)` would infer). No `@requires`: it
-- performs nothing.
@native
@label "Derive traverse (bridge)"
@description "Phase 6d — the reflection + marshal bridge behind `Traversable.traverse`: resolves the dispatched value's owning type and the applicative `g` (from `f`'s declared return type, else a first element), marshals the schema, and delegates the sequencing to `deriveTraverseFold` / `deriveTraverseList`. Returns the value unchanged when the applicative cannot be resolved. Implemented by a context native of the `derive-functor` container."
@tags "engine" "traversable" "derive" "kinds" "phase-6d"
deriveTraverse : (f: a -> b) -> (value: c) -> Any

-- deriveTraverseFold — the entry (the `$tag`-record / variant arm). `f` the
-- effectful fn, `value` the runtime functor value, `schemaView` the dispatched
-- type's schema marshalled to TraversalType, `paramName` the functor type-param
-- name, `typeName` the owning type-constructor name (self-recursion detection),
-- `pureFn`/`apFn` the resolved applicative `g`'s handles. (The array repr is
-- handled by deriveTraverseList, called directly by the bridge.)
@label "Derive traverse (generic sequence)"
@description "Phase 6d — the generic schema-directed `traverse`: any `* -> *` type without an authored Traversable instance gets traverse free. Sequences the functor-param leaves (TtVar paramName) with the threaded applicative, recurses self-recursive fields (TtNamed typeName), re-dispatches one-level nested foreign functors (TtApp carrying the param), leaves the rest. The decision half of the derived Traversable instance; the engine:deriveTraverse bridge supplies (f, value, schemaView, paramName, typeName, pureFn, apFn) — pureFn/apFn the resolved applicative g (D-6d-2). Total: descends only into strictly-smaller self-recursive sub-values."
@tags "engine" "traversable" "derive" "kinds" "phase-6d"
deriveTraverseFold : (f: a) -> (value: b) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> (pureFn: c) -> (apFn: d) -> e
deriveTraverseFold f value schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn =
  case schemaView of
    TtOpaque { pure = p } -> deriveTraverseFold f value p paramName typeName pureFn apFn
    TtRefined { base = bse } -> deriveTraverseFold f value bse paramName typeName pureFn apFn
    TtMu { body = bdy } -> deriveTraverseFold f value bdy paramName typeName pureFn apFn
    TtRecord { fields = fs } ->
      deriveTraverseFields f value fs schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn
    TtVariant { cases = cs } ->
      case mapGet value "$tag" of
        Nothing -> pureFn $ value
        Just tag ->
          case deriveTraverseFindCase cs tag of
            Nothing -> pureFn $ value
            Just c -> deriveTraverseFields f value c.fields schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn
    _ -> pureFn $ value

-- deriveTraverseFindCase — locate the variant case whose name matches the value's
-- `$tag`. Internal helper; head/tail recursion (the array-repr List idiom).
@label "derive-traversable: findCase"
@description "Phase 6d — locate the TtVariantCase matching the value's $tag. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseFindCase : (cases: List a) -> (tag: String) -> Maybe a
deriveTraverseFindCase cases tag =
  case head cases of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just c ->
      if eq c.name tag
        then Just c
        else case tail cases of
          Nothing -> Nothing
          Just rest -> deriveTraverseFindCase rest tag

-- deriveTraverseFields — sequence a case's fields. Start the accumulator at
-- `pureFn $ value` (the original value in `g`, preserving $tag + untouched
-- fields), then thread it left-to-right combining each traversed field. Internal.
@label "derive-traversable: fields"
@description "Phase 6d — sequence a case's fields: acc starts at `pureFn value` (g-wrapped original), each traversed field is combined via ap. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseFields : (f: a) -> (value: b) -> (fields: List c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> (pureFn: d) -> (apFn: e) -> g
deriveTraverseFields f value fields schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn =
  deriveTraverseFieldsGo f (pureFn $ value) value fields schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn

-- deriveTraverseFieldsGo — the accumulator-threaded fold behind deriveTraverseFields.
@label "derive-traversable: fieldsGo"
@description "Phase 6d — accumulator-threaded fold: walk the declared fields, combine each traversed field's effect onto the g-accumulator via ap. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseFieldsGo : (f: a) -> (acc: g) -> (value: b) -> (fields: List c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> (pureFn: d) -> (apFn: e) -> g
deriveTraverseFieldsGo f acc value fields schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just fld ->
      let acc2 = deriveTraverseStepField f acc value fld schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn
      case tail fields of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> deriveTraverseFieldsGo f acc2 value rest schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn

-- deriveTraverseStepField — one field step. A field absent from the value (a
-- partial record) leaves the accumulator untouched; else classify+combine it.
-- Split out to avoid a `case`-in-`let` (the analyze.fenel/totality.fenel idiom).
@label "derive-traversable: stepField"
@description "Phase 6d — one field: read the value's field (absent ⇒ leave acc), classify+combine its effect onto acc. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseStepField : (f: a) -> (acc: g) -> (value: b) -> (fld: c) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> (pureFn: d) -> (apFn: e) -> g
deriveTraverseStepField f acc value fld schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn =
  case mapGet value fld.name of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just fieldVal ->
      deriveTraverseCombineField f acc fld.name fieldVal fld.type schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn

-- deriveTraverseCombineField — CLASSIFY one field by its marshalled TraversalType,
-- and (when it traverses) produce its `g`-wrapped value `gNew` + combine onto acc:
--   element        — `TtVar paramName`  ⇒ `f $ fieldVal` (`g b`).
--   self-recursive — `TtNamed typeName` ⇒ recurse `deriveTraverseFold` (`g (f b)`).
--   nested functor — `TtApp` carrying the param ⇒ re-dispatch `Traversable.traverse`
--                    on the field value (D-6d-4, one level; nominal for List/Maybe,
--                    derived for a user functor).
--   map-field      — `TtMap` whose values carry the param ⇒ `mapTraverse f` over
--                    the map's values (D-6c-3, closed Phase 1a — a direct call,
--                    the bare map field has no `$tag` to re-dispatch on).
--   otherwise (a different var / fixed type / compound-nested TtApp / TtMap)
--            ⇒ LEAVE acc unchanged (the field stays as in the pureFn-wrapped value).
@label "derive-traversable: combineField"
@description "Phase 6d/1a — classify a field by its TraversalType: TtVar paramName ⇒ f the value (g b); TtNamed typeName ⇒ recurse (self-recursive); TtApp carrying the param ⇒ re-dispatch Traversable.traverse on the nested functor value (D-6d-4, one level); TtMap whose values carry the param ⇒ mapTraverse f over the map values (D-6c-3, closed Phase 1a); else leave. Combine the traversed effect onto the g-accumulator via deriveTraverseAp. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseCombineField : (f: a) -> (acc: g) -> (fldName: String) -> (fieldVal: b) -> (ft: TraversalType) -> (schemaView: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> (typeName: String) -> (pureFn: d) -> (apFn: e) -> g
deriveTraverseCombineField f acc fldName fieldVal ft schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn =
  case ft of
    TtVar { name = vn } ->
      if eq vn paramName
        then deriveTraverseAp apFn acc fldName (f $ fieldVal)
        else acc
    TtNamed { name = nn } ->
      if eq nn typeName
        then deriveTraverseAp apFn acc fldName (deriveTraverseFold f fieldVal schemaView paramName typeName pureFn apFn)
        else acc
    TtApp { args = as } ->
      if deriveTraverseAppHasParam as paramName
        then deriveTraverseAp apFn acc fldName (traverse f fieldVal)
        else acc
    TtMap { values = vs } ->
      if deriveTraverseArgIsParam vs paramName
        then deriveTraverseAp apFn acc fldName (mapTraverse f fieldVal)
        else acc
    _ -> acc

-- deriveTraverseAp — combine one traversed field's effect onto the accumulator:
-- lift a one-field SETTER over acc (`g (nv -> value)`) via the g-Functor, then
-- `ap` it against `gNew` (`g nv`) ⇒ `g value'` with `fldName` set to the traversed
-- value. Internal helper.
@label "derive-traversable: ap"
@description "Phase 6d — combine a traversed field onto the g-accumulator: fmap a one-field setter over acc, then ap against the field's g-wrapped value. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseAp : (apFn: e) -> (acc: g) -> (fldName: String) -> (gNew: g) -> g
deriveTraverseAp apFn acc fldName gNew =
  let setterG = fmap (deriveTraverseSetter fldName) acc
  (apFn $ setterG) $ gNew

-- deriveTraverseSetter — the one-field record setter (curried: fldName, the
-- record `v`, the new value `nv`). `fmap (deriveTraverseSetter fldName) acc`
-- collects [fldName, v] leaving `nv -> record'`; `ap` supplies `nv`. Internal.
@label "derive-traversable: setter"
@description "Phase 6d — one-field record setter: assoc nv onto v at fldName. Curried so fmap+ap thread it. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseSetter : (fldName: String) -> (v: a) -> (nv: b) -> a
deriveTraverseSetter fldName v nv = assocRecord v fldName nv

-- deriveTraverseAppHasParam — does this applied-type's arg list carry the functor
-- param DIRECTLY (one-level nesting)? A nested TtApp arg (compound nesting,
-- `List (Box a)`) does NOT count — the D-6d-4 fence. Internal helper.
@label "derive-traversable: appHasParam"
@description "Phase 6d — does an applied-type's arg list carry the functor param directly (one-level nesting)? A nested TtApp arg (compound nesting) does NOT count — D-6d-4 fence. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseAppHasParam : (args: List a) -> (paramName: String) -> Bool
deriveTraverseAppHasParam args paramName =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> false
    Just a ->
      if deriveTraverseArgIsParam a paramName
        then true
        else case tail args of
          Nothing -> false
          Just rest -> deriveTraverseAppHasParam rest paramName

-- deriveTraverseArgIsParam — is this single TraversalType arg the functor param
-- (`TtVar paramName`)? Internal helper.
@label "derive-traversable: argIsParam"
@description "Phase 6d — is a single TraversalType arg the functor param (TtVar paramName)? Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseArgIsParam : (a: TraversalType) -> (paramName: String) -> Bool
deriveTraverseArgIsParam a paramName =
  case a of
    TtVar { name = vn } -> eq vn paramName
    _ -> false

-- deriveTraverseList — the array-repr arm (`List`'s `$opaque` array carries no
-- `$tag`, so the schema-fold can't reach it — the 6c Foldable List precedent).
-- `traverse f [] = pure []`; `traverse f (x:xs) = ap (fmap prepend (f x)) (traverse f xs)`.
-- The bridge calls THIS directly when the dispatched value is a JS array; it
-- re-dispatches via plain recursion (NOT `Traversable.traverse`) so it stays in
-- the array arm and reuses the threaded `pureFn`/`apFn`.
@label "derive-traversable: list"
@description "Phase 6d — the array-repr arm: traverse a List left-to-right, sequencing with the threaded applicative. `traverse f [] = pure []`; `traverse f (x:xs) = ap (fmap (:) (f x)) (traverse f xs)`. Called by the engine:deriveTraverse bridge for JS arrays. Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "list" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseList : (f: a) -> (xs: List b) -> (pureFn: c) -> (apFn: d) -> g
deriveTraverseList f xs pureFn apFn =
  case head xs of
    Nothing -> pureFn $ []
    Just x -> deriveTraverseListCons f x (tail xs) pureFn apFn

-- deriveTraverseListCons — the cons step: prepend the head's traversed effect onto
-- the recursively-traversed tail, all inside `g`. Internal helper.
@label "derive-traversable: listCons"
@description "Phase 6d — the List cons step: ap (fmap prepend (f x)) (traverse f rest). Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "list" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraverseListCons : (f: a) -> (x: b) -> (maybeRest: Maybe (List b)) -> (pureFn: c) -> (apFn: d) -> g
deriveTraverseListCons f x maybeRest pureFn apFn =
  let consG = fmap deriveTraversePrepend (f $ x)
  case maybeRest of
    Nothing -> (apFn $ consG) $ (pureFn $ [])
    Just rest -> (apFn $ consG) $ (deriveTraverseList f rest pureFn apFn)

-- deriveTraversePrepend — cons an element onto the front of a list (the List
-- traverse's element-order builder). Curried so fmap+ap thread it. Internal.
@label "derive-traversable: prepend"
@description "Phase 6d — cons an element onto the front of a list (List traverse's builder). Helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "traversable" "list" "phase-6d"
@category "engine-internal"
deriveTraversePrepend : (y: a) -> (ys: List a) -> List a
deriveTraversePrepend y ys = concat [y] ys
